            <ArticleTitle>[The Social Experience of Being Obese. Obesity Prevention of Socially Deprived Adolescents].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S29-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0033-1333710</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Group discussions with obese teenagers and parents with obese children are the empirical basis of this research project. The results indicate that 'being fat' is primarily a social experience. Consequently, preventive measures to inhibit unhealthy lifestyle habits fail to go into sufficient depth. Overweight adolescents call for equality; they demand a more equal treatment in social interactions and relations.</AbstractText>
